POSTGRES_USER=postgres
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=postgres
POSTGRES_DB=appdb


# Replace the placeholder values with your real credentials locally (do NOT commit)
POSTGRES_USER=your_db_user
POSTGRES_PASSWORD=your_db_password
POSTGRES_DB=your_db_name
# Example DATABASE_URL format: postgresql://user:password@host:5432/dbname
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://your_db_user:your_db_password@db:5432/your_db_name

docker create --name temp-prisma-debug --network pipeline_default node:20-bullseye sleep infinity
docker cp .\scripts\prisma_repro\. temp-prisma-debug:/work
docker start temp-prisma-debug
docker exec temp-prisma-debug bash -lc "cd /work && npm init -y >/dev/null && npm i --no-audit --no-fund prisma@7.4.2 --silent && echo '--- prisma version ---' && npx prisma --version && echo '--- running migrate deploy ---' && DEBUG=prisma:* npx prisma migrate deploy --schema=./schema.prisma"
docker rm -f temp-prisma-debug

### Historical: Prisma debug steps (optional)

The commands above document an experimental attempt to run Prisma migrations inside
a transient container (left here for posterity / optional debugging). During
development we encountered parser, runtime-config, and Windows/docker path
issues; those experiments did not become the project's primary flow.

If you want to reproduce that approach for troubleshooting, the steps are
available above. They are optional — the project now uses the idempotent SQL
migration runner in `scripts/apply_sql_migration_neon.sh` and the SQL files in
`scripts/sql/migrations/` to initialize or migrate the database.

Preferred (current) workflow:

1) Set `DATABASE_URL` to your local compose or hosted DB.

2) Run the idempotent SQL runner:

```bash
export DATABASE_URL="postgresql://your_db_user:your_db_password@db:5432/your_db_name"
./scripts/apply_sql_migration_neon.sh
```

3) Start the app as usual with `docker compose up` or your local dev flow.

Keep the Prisma repro commands above only if you want to try the older path.
